{% doc %}
  Press Grid Block

  One six-item unit of the Press Grid — a 2x2 featured cell plus five 1x1 cards, laid out as a single
  3x3 grid on desktop and a stacked column on mobile. Shared verbatim by the News & TVCs blog view and
  the All News archive, which is why both the mirror and the source are parameters rather than layouts.

  One grid, not nested ones: every 1x1 card is a real cell of the same track, so the five of them are
  identical at any width and the featured cell is exactly two of them plus the gap. Figma's own numbers
  confirm the single 24px gap on both axes: the featured 644 is 310 + 24 + 310.

  The grid's Figma card is 424x310 — a 154 media over a 154 body between 1px borders — where the nav
  pane's media is 160. press-card defaults to the nav's, so the grid passes its own.

  lg:auto-rows-fr equalises the three rows. Without it the last row sizes to its own cards, and a
  three-line headline there makes its cards taller than the two beside the featured cell.

  Column width is never declared. lg:grid-cols-3 with lg:gap-6 derives 424 on the 1320 content width,
  and the featured cell's lg:col-span-2 derives 872 — correct at any container width.

  The featured cell's height is the two rows it spans plus the gap, so the side cards define it and
  the 2x2 stays exactly 2x2. It takes the Figma's 218/161 only when there are no side cards to derive
  that from: a grid item carrying a ratio is not stretched to its span, and it transfers the ratio
  back into a minimum width, which lg:min-w-0 keeps from blowing the cell out over its neighbours.

  Mirroring moves the cells with lg:col-start-*, never flex-row-reverse or order, so DOM order stays
  reading order and the tab sequence survives the flip.

  Every cell in the first two rows is placed explicitly. Auto-placement only moves forward, so a side
  card left to find its own cell would drop below a mirrored featured cell instead of beside it.

  Two sources feed the same layout. Blocks are merchant-authored on the Press Grid section, so items
  are block objects. Articles are the paginated archive, and because Liquid cannot build an array of
  objects the caller filters to handles and passes the array they resolve against as block_source.

  This snippet only places cells. press-grid-card owns every source-to-primitive mapping, so the
  featured cell and the five standard cards resolve their fields through exactly the same path.

  @param {object[]} block_items - Up to five standard items: blocks when block_kind is 'block', handles when 'article' (required)
  @param {object} [block_lead] - The 2x2 hero item. Without one the grid degrades to a plain 3-column run
  @param {string} block_kind - 'block' or 'article' (required)
  @param {article[]} [block_source] - The article array handles resolve against. Required when block_kind is 'article'
  @param {boolean} [block_mirrored] - Place the featured cell on the right (default: false)
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign block_items = block_items | default: blank
  assign block_lead = block_lead | default: blank

  unless block_items != blank or block_lead != blank
    break
  endunless

  if block_mirrored
    assign block_lead_position = 'lg:col-start-2'
    assign block_side_position = 'lg:col-start-1'
  else
    assign block_lead_position = 'lg:col-start-1'
    assign block_side_position = 'lg:col-start-3'
  endif

  # The 2x2 cell is what makes the lead row a lead row; with no hero every item is just a card
  if block_lead != blank
    assign block_side_items = block_items | slice: 0, 2
    if block_items.size > 2
      assign block_rest_items = block_items | slice: 2, 3
    else
      assign block_rest_items = blank
    endif
  else
    assign block_side_items = blank
    assign block_rest_items = block_items
  endif

  assign block_lead_shape = ''
  if block_side_items == blank
    assign block_lead_shape = 'lg:aspect-[218/161]'
  endif
-%}

<div class="press-grid-block flex flex-col gap-4 lg:grid lg:auto-rows-fr lg:grid-cols-3 lg:gap-6">
  {%- if block_lead != blank -%}
    <div class="press-grid-block__featured hidden lg:relative lg:col-span-2 lg:row-span-2 lg:row-start-1 lg:block lg:min-w-0 {{ block_lead_shape }} {{ block_lead_position }}">
      {%- render 'press-grid-card',
        card_item: block_lead,
        card_kind: block_kind,
        card_variant: 'featured',
        card_source: block_source
      -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- for block_item in block_side_items -%}
    {%- liquid
      if forloop.first
        assign block_side_row = 'lg:row-start-1'
      else
        assign block_side_row = 'lg:row-start-2'
      endif
    -%}
    <div class="press-grid-block__side {{ block_side_row }} {{ block_side_position }}">
      {%- render 'press-grid-card',
        card_item: block_item,
        card_kind: block_kind,
        card_source: block_source,
        card_media_class: 'h-[154px]'
      -%}
    </div>
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- for block_item in block_rest_items -%}
    {%- render 'press-grid-card',
      card_item: block_item,
      card_kind: block_kind,
      card_source: block_source,
      card_media_class: 'h-[154px]'
    -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
</div>
